 9 Model Evaluation and Further Discussion
                               众


 9.1 Evaluation of Models
                                                                  m
                       公


                                                    H
      The decomposition of microorganisms is a very important part in the carbon cycle. By
 establishing models of wood decomposition and fungal growth, we have perfectly met the
                                                 AT
       信




 requirements of question, drawing a series of conclusions about the impact of environmental
 changes on bacterial species and the importance of biodiversity.
      During our modeling process, we set reasonable assumptions to simplify our models. Also,
      微

                                          M


 we take the sensitivity analysis which verified the stability of the models.
      The specific advantages of our models are as follows:
                                 ：




 ⚫   We adopt the Logistics growth model with the competition among fungi including in the
     model, so as to simulate the interaction between species well. Moreover, we reasonably
                        号




     analyze the advantages and dis advantages of species with different characteristics in various
     environments.
 ⚫   The calculation of unknown parameters is scientific. Reasonable training set and test set help
                信




     us make sure the accuracy of parameters.
      However, our models still have the following weaknesses:
       微




 ⚫   Our hypothesis only considers two parameters affecting fungal decomposition, ignoring
     endogenous and exogenous factors.




